{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1092189-dark-ages-ratkin","id":1092189,"title":"Dark Ages Ratkin","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-13T19:38:17-07:00","id":1092189,"title":"Dark Ages Ratkin","content":"So, planning to use Ratkin in the Dark Ages setting. Aside from the game mechanics of Abilities, what else do people think need changing?<br /> <br /> Obviously, the 1200s are well after the War of Rage and the extinction of the Bards, so the remaining four Aspects (Tunnel Runners, Shadow Seets, Knife Skulkers and Warriors) are all available. But what about the Freak Aspects?<br /> <br /> I think the Freak Factor background should be available, but not all the Freak Aspects themselves.<br /> Engineers \u2013 no, I don\u2019t think should be available in any form.<br /> Plague Lords \u2013 definitely available, as the <b>Ratkin Changing Breed</b> book explicitly states that they helped spread the Black Plague through Europe in the 1300s.<br /> Munchmausen \u2013 Maybe? Their sense of adventure seems out-of-place for the time period, but otherwise they seem fine.<br /> Twitchers \u2013 Probably not available. Their sense of paranoia and end-time hysteria does not really fit the Dark Ages.<br /> <br /> Aside from those changes, the big thing to consider would be the Plagues. Dark Ages European Ratkin are probably organised differently to those in the Final Nights. Perhaps the Plagues are grouped by country rather than continent? Or if not country, \u2018region\u2019, maybe divided up as the chapters of <b>Dark Ages: Europe</b>, for example?<br /> <br /> It may also be worth re-tooling the Colony background, reducing the Ratkin population for the Dark Ages?<br /> <br /> Nest rating Number of Ratkin Description<br /> One 1-3<br /> Two 4-10<br /> Three 11-20<br /> Four 21-40<br /> Five 40+<br /> <br /> Anyone think of anything else, or have an opinion on what I have so far?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5922-volesus","name":"Volesus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5922_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T03:14:43-07:00","id":1092291,"title":"","content":"The Munchmausen wouldn't have that name yet, so I would make them rare urban legend sorts referred to as Moon Mice.<br /> <br /> I perhaps if you want twitchers are also rare and emerging, after all millennial fever is t just unique to the 2000 crowd, and paranoia is also an old old problem. Maybe twitchers only pop up one in a thousand or so.<br /> <br /> <br /> I can see Ratkin having huge migrations following the plagues, so you could have Nezumi bring plague rats from the Mongol Hordes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T07:48:11-07:00","id":1092328,"title":"","content":"Having run Ratkin in a DA:W game, I agree with most of the changes you propose.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Volesus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1092189-dark-ages-ratkin#post1092189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I think the Freak Factor background should be available, but not all the Freak Aspects themselves.<br /> Engineers \u2013 no, I don\u2019t think should be available in any form.<br /> Plague Lords \u2013 definitely available, as the <b>Ratkin Changing Breed</b> book explicitly states that they helped spread the Black Plague through Europe in the 1300s.<br /> Munchmausen \u2013 Maybe? Their sense of adventure seems out-of-place for the time period, but otherwise they seem fine.<br /> Twitchers \u2013 Probably not available. Their sense of paranoia and end-time hysteria does not really fit the Dark Ages.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually don't see a problem with having any of the Freak Aspects available. Though they would be extremely rare. The Plague Lords being the most common among them. But you don't lose much from banning the Engineers and/or Twitchers outright.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Volesus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1092189-dark-ages-ratkin#post1092189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Aside from those changes, the big thing to consider would be the Plagues. Dark Ages European Ratkin are probably organised differently to those in the Final Nights. Perhaps the Plagues are grouped by country rather than continent? Or if not country, \u2018region\u2019, maybe divided up as the chapters of <b>Dark Ages: Europe</b>, for example?</div> </div> </div> </div>This I wouldn't change. I don't see a problem with having 99% of the Ratkin in the Chronicle belong to the same Plague. The Ratkin don't really swear loyalty to a Plague after all. For them it's more of a smaller scale Colony thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Volesus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1092189-dark-ages-ratkin#post1092189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It may also be worth re-tooling the Colony background, reducing the Ratkin population for the Dark Ages?<br /> <br /> Nest rating Number of Ratkin Description<br /> One 1-3<br /> Two 4-10<br /> Three 11-20<br /> Four 21-40<br /> Five 40+</div> </div> </div> </div>If this works for you, go for it. By the Dark Ages, the Ratkin have been working on building their numbers for a few millenia. And depending on story requirements (if this isn't a pure Ratkin game) I don't know that this will come up as terribly important. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Volesus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1092189-dark-ages-ratkin#post1092189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Anyone think of anything else, or have an opinion on what I have so far?</div> </div> </div> </div>Opinions stated above. But good luck and have fun. And don't get bogged down in the details if you don't need to.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T14:01:44-07:00","id":1095233,"title":"","content":"I'd say Engineers are fine, they'd just be focused on period technology and engineering.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}